CRASHER 1 — bicep adapter panic (found by go fuzz, FuzzBicep, 2026-10-12)

Input (15 bytes, this directory's .input file):
  resource A0'''0

Panic:
  runtime error: slice bounds out of range [:18] with length 15

Stack (abridged):
  aegis/internal/adapter/bicep/bicep.go:201 in (*parser).parseKeyword
  aegis/internal/adapter/bicep/bicep.go:373 in (*parser).parseResource

Root cause (read-only analysis):
  parseStringVal treats ''' as a multiline-string opener. On unterminated
  input the scan loop exits at EOF, then `p.pos += 3` (bicep.go ~line 258)
  blindly skips the never-found closing delimiter, leaving p.pos (18) past
  len(src) (15). The next parseKeyword does p.src[start:p.pos] = p.src[18:18]
  and panics.

Repro (Go):
  ad := bicep.Adapter{}
  _, _, _ = ad.Parse("main.bicep", []byte("resource A0'''0"))  // panics

Production impact: CONTAINED. CLI and `aegis serve` wrap adapter Parse in
safeParse/safeParseModule panic recovery, so this surfaces as a
"parse failed ... panicked" error diagnostic, not a process crash
(verified live against `aegis serve` — HTTP 200 + diagnostic, no stack
trace leaked, server stays up).

Severity: Medium (parser robustness defect; unguarded slice arithmetic;
any future caller that skips the recover wrapper would crash).
